{
  "description": "#6742 — a query block runs the tokens the search box runs. Each pair of steps is one text: `search_*` is the request the search box sends for it and `block_*` the one a query block compiles it to (`compileQueryText`, pinned to these args by `query-text-conformance.test.ts`, which also holds each pair to the same rows). `path:` is a `PathGlob` over the title of the block's page, so it keeps every block on the page as search does, not the page row alone; `under:` is `TagUnder`, the tag attached (S2), inherited (S3, under S2) or written inline (S7); free text is the request's `fulltext`; a relative date is the dates it names on the day the query runs, here `overdue` against a due date in 2020 and one in 2999 so the rows do not move with the clock. Content arrives through `edit_block`, since only an op fills `fts_blocks` and `block_tag_refs`.",
